    "narrative": "The anchor for today\u2019s lineup is undoubtedly **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who carries an elite 85.34 score into a favorable matchup against Whisenhunt. Facing a sub-par 5.60 xERA pitcher while hitting second in the order provides the perfect environment for a high-ceiling performance in both R and RBI categories. Joining him as a priority start is **Daulton Varsho** (70.98), who benefits significantly from an exploitation of the platoon split against Klassen. While **Bryce Harper** (65.42) draws a neutral-to-difficult matchup against Gibson, his elite xwOBA metrics and prime position in the three-hole make him a must-start despite the inherent risk of a lefty-lefty matchup. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Braden Montgomery**; while his 47.71 score is modest, the favorable wind conditions at the park provide just enough of an upside boost to justify his inclusion over our deeper bench options.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision of the day involved **Gleyber Torres** (38.19), who narrowly missed our 40-point threshold for active play. While his leadoff position provided a +10% boost to his projection, the combination of a tough matchup against Ashcraft and a significant penalty for the platoon split effectively neutralized his upside. We similarly opted to sideline **Brendan Donovan** (36.40), as the matchup against Harrison remains unfavorable for his current offensive profile. We continue to monitor the status of **Will Smith** and **Matt Chapman**, both of whom remain sidelined with injuries, further tightening our options for the utility slots. As we navigate the schedule, we remain wary of the volatility surrounding **Yainer Diaz** and **JJ Bleday**, both of whom see their scores tempered by either bottom-of-the-order positioning or unfavorable platoon dynamics. With our remaining depth including **Tyler Freeman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Alex Freeland**, we are well-positioned to pivot should any late-inning weather alerts or lineup shuffles materialize.",
